Article 1 (Purpose ) The purpose of this Decree is to prescribe matters mandated by the Act on the Promotion of Quantum Science and Technology and Quantum Industry and matters necessary for enforcing that Act.

Article 2 (Procedures for formulation of comprehensive quantum plans ) (1) When the Minister of Science and ICT formulates a comprehensive plan for the promotion of quantum science and technology and the quantum industry (hereinafter referred to as "comprehensive quantum plan") under Article 5(1) of the Act on the Promotion of Quantum Science and Technology and Quantum Industry (hereinafter referred to as the "Act"), the Minister shall prepare a draft comprehensive quantum plan and notify the heads of the relevant central administrative agencies thereof no later than August 30 of the year preceding the year in which the planned period of the comprehensive quantum plan begins.
  (2) The head of the relevant central administrative agency who has received the notification under paragraph (1) shall submit matters to be reflected in the relevant comprehensive quantum plan to the Minister of Science and ICT within 30 days from the date of receiving the notification.
  (3) "Where any modification concerns minor matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso of Article 5(4) of the Act means any of the following:
  1. Where it is intended to modify the comprehensive quantum plan to the extent not to change the purpose and performance indicators of the comprehensive quantum plan, the deadlines for achieving the objectives, etc.
  2. Where it is intended to change terms, etc. in accordance with the amendment or change of other statutes, regulations, plans, etc.;
  3. Where it is intended to correct a simple mistake, misrepresentation, omission, or obvious error corresponding thereto.
  (4) Where the Minister of Science and ICT finalizes or modifies the comprehensive quantum plan, the Minister shall notify the head of the relevant central administrative agency thereof within 10 days; provided, the Minister may notify the head of the relevant central administrative agency thereof, except for matters deemed necessary to maintain confidentiality for the protection of national security, advanced technologies, and industries.

Article 3 (Procedures for formulation of implementation plans) (1) Where the Minister of Science and ICT formulates an annual implementation plan under Article 6(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "implementation plan"), the Minister shall prepare a draft implementation plan and notify the heads of the relevant central administrative agencies thereof no later than August 30 of the year preceding the year in which the implementation plan begins.
  (2) The head of the relevant central administrative agency who has received the notification under paragraph (1) shall submit matters to be reflected in the implementation plan to the Minister of Science and ICT within 30 days from the date of receiving the notification.
  (3) The Minister of Science and ICT shall formulate an implementation plan by reflecting the matters submitted under paragraph (2) and report it to the Quantum Strategy Committee under Article 7(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Quantum Strategy Committee").
  (4) The Minister of Science and ICT may modify the implementation plan where necessary to incorporate changes made to the comprehensive quantum plan or where modification of the implementation plan is otherwise required due to changes in the domestic or international circumstances, etc.
  (5) Where the Minister of Science and ICT modifies the implementation plan under paragraph (4), the Minister shall report to the working committee under Article 7(4) of the Act.
  (6) Where the Minister of Science and ICT finalizes or modifies the implementation plan, the Minister shall notify the heads of relevant central administrative agencies within 10 days; provided, matters deemed necessary to remain confidential for the protection of national security, advanced technologies, industries, or similar interests may be excluded from the notification.

Article 4 (Composition and operation of Quantum Strategy Committee) (1) “Head of a relevant central administrative agency prescribed by Presidential Decree“ in Article 7(3)1 of the Act means each of the heads of the following central administrative agencies:
  1. The Minister of Economy and Finance;
  2 2. The Ministry of Education;
  3. The Minister of Foreign Affairs;
  4 4. The Minister of National Defense;
  5. The Minister of Trade, Industry and Energy;
  6. The Minister of SMEs and Startups;
  7. The Director of the National Intelligence Service;
  8. Any other head of a central administrative agency whom the chairperson of the Quantum Strategy Committee (hereinafter referred to as the "chairperson") recognizes as having work-related relevance to agenda items submitted to the Quantum Strategy Committee.
  (2) The terms of office of members commissioned under Article 7(3)2 of the Act shall be 2 years.
  (3) The term of office of a newly commissioned member due to the resignation, etc. of a commissioned member under Article 7(3)2 of the Act shall be the remaining term of office of the former member.
  (4) Where a member commissioned under Article 7(3)2 of the Act falls within any of the following categories, the chairperson may remove the relevant member:
  1. Where the member becomes unable to perform his or her duties for a long time due to mental or physical weakness, etc.;
  2. Where the member commits any misconduct in connection with his or her duties;
  3. Where the member is deemed unsuitable to serve as a member due to neglect of duty, injury to dignity, or any other reason;
  4. Where the member voluntarily expresses that it is difficult for him or her to perform the duties.
  (5) The chairperson shall convene and preside over meetings of the Quantum Strategy Committee.
  (6) A majority of the members of the Quantum Strategy Committee shall constitute a quorum; and any decision thereof shall require the concurring vote of at least a majority of those present.
  (7) Where the chairperson is unable to perform his or her duties, the vice chairperson shall act on behalf of the chairperson when the chairperson is unable to perform his or her duties.
  (8) If the chairperson deems it necessary for deliberation, the chairperson may request the heads of relevant institutions or relevant experts to attend a meeting to hear their opinions.
  (9) The Minister of Science and ICT shall assist the chairperson and, under the direction of the chairperson, oversee the affairs of the Quantum Strategy Committee.
  (10) The Minister of Science and ICT may have public officials under his or her jurisdiction support the operation of the Quantum Strategy Committee for the efficient performance of the affairs of the Quantum Strategy Committee.

Article 5 (Composition and operation of working committee) (1) The working committee under Article 7(4) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "working committee") shall be comprised of up to 20 members appointed or commissioned by the Minister of Science and ICT from among the following persons. In such cases, the civilian members shall constitute a majority of all the members:
  1. A public officials of Grade III or higher (including public officials who are members of the Senior Executive Service) of the relevant central administrative agency under Article 4 (1)1 through 7, designated by the head of the relevant agency;
  2. A person who is or has been an associate professor or higher in a field related to quantum science and technology or quantum enabling technology at a university;
  3. A person who is or has been employed for at least 5 years at a research institute in the field of quantum science and technology or quantum enabling technology;
  4. A person who is or has been employed for at least 5 years as an executive officer or employee in the quantum-related industry;
  5. A person who has expertise in the impact analysis of quantum science and technology or the review of security threat factors under Article 10 of the Act;
  6. Any other person recognized by the Minister of Science and ICT as having expertise in quantum science and technology and the quantum industry.
  (2) The chairperson and vice chairperson of the working committee shall be persons designated by the Minister of Science and ICT.
  (3) The term of office of the members commissioned under paragraph (1) shall be 2 years.
  (4) The term of office of a member newly commissioned due to the resignation of a member commissioned under paragraph (1) or for any other reason shall be the remaining term of office of the predecessor.
  (5) Where any subparagraph of Article 4(4) applies to a member commissioned under paragraph (1), the Minister of Science and ICT may remove the relevant member.
  (6) Where the Quantum Strategy Committee intends to delegate the deliberation of an agenda item to the working committee under Article 7(4) of the Act, it shall undergo deliberation and resolution by the Quantum Strategy Committee.
  (7) The chairperson of the working committee may, if deemed necessary for deliberation, request public officials of relevant agencies or related experts to attend a meeting to hear their opinions.
  (8) The Minister of Science and ICT shall oversee the affairs of the working committee and may have public officials under his or her jurisdiction support the operation of the working committee for the efficient performance of the affairs of the working committee.

Article 6 (Composition and operation of expert committees) (1) The Quantum Strategy Committee may establish an expert committee comprised of experts from enterprises, research institutes, universities, etc. to support the Quantum Strategy Committee and its working committee under Article 7(5) of the Act.
  (2) The expert committee shall be comprised of up to 20 members commissioned by the Minister of Science and ICT, and the chairperson of the expert committee shall be designated by the Minister of Science and ICT from among the members of the expert committee.
  (3) When the chairperson of the expert committee deems it necessary for deliberation, the chairperson may request public officials of related agencies or relevant experts to attend a meeting to hear their opinions.

Article 7 (Allowances and travel expenses for Quantum Strategy Committee) Members, public officials, and experts attending meetings of the Quantum Strategy Committee, the working committee, the expert committee may be paid allowances, travel expenses, and other necessary expenses within the budget; provided, this shall not apply where public officials attending meetings in direct connection with their assigned duties.

Article 8 (Methods of fact-finding surveys) (1) Statistical surveys or fact-finding surveys under Article 8(1) of the Act may be conducted in various ways, such as written surveys, literature reviews, and the solicitation of expert opinions on the following matters:
  1. Current status of domestic and international technologies and related industries;
  2. Current status of domestic and international workforce;
  3. Current status of related entities, such as domestic and international companies;
  4. Current status of intellectual property, including domestic and international patents:
  5. Major domestic and international standards and current status of standards;
  6. Major trends in domestic and international legal and international frameworks;
  7. Other matters deemed necessary by the Minister of Science and ICT for the effective formulation of policies on quantum science and technology and the quantum industry.
  (2) The Minister of Science and ICT shall report the results of statistical surveys or fact-finding surveys conducted under paragraph (1) to the working committee.
  (3) The Minister of Science and ICT may, in accordance with Article 8(3) of the Act, entrust all or part of the task of performing statistical surveys or fact-finding surveys to any of the following institutions or organizations:
  1. A research and development institute under subparagraph 3 of Article 2 of the National Research and Development Innovation Act;
  2. A specialized institution under subparagraph 4 of Article 2 of the National Research and Development Innovation Act;
  1. A public institution under Article 4 of the Act on the Management of Public Institutions;
  4. A non-profit corporation permitted to be established by the Minister of Science and ICT under Article 32 of the Civil Act and Article 4 of the Act on the Establishment and Operation of Public Interest Corporations;
  5. The National Information Society Agency for Intelligent Information Society established under Article 12 of the Framework Act on Intelligent Informatization;
  6. Any other institution or organization recognized by the Minister of Science and ICT as having specialized personnel and dedicated organizations related to quantum science and technology or the quantum industry.
  (4) Where the Minister of Science and ICT entrusts the task under paragraph (3), the Minister shall publish the entrusted person and the details of the entrusted task in the Official Gazette.

Article 9 (Entrustment of tasks of establishing and operating quantum science and technology information system) (1) The Minister of Science and ICT may, in accordance with Article 9 (2) of the Act, entrust all or part of the task of establishing or operating the quantum science and technology information system to any of the following institutions or organizations:
  1. A research and development institute under subparagraph 3 of Article 2 of the National Research and Development Innovation Act;
  2. A specialized institution under subparagraph 4 of Article 2 of the National Research and Development Innovation Act;
  3. A public institution under Article 4 of the Act on the Management of Public Institutions;
  4. A non-profit corporation permitted to be established by the Minister of Science and ICT under Article 32 of the Civil Act and Article 4 of the Act on the Establishment and Operation of Public Interest Corporations;
  5. The National Information Society Agency for Intelligent Information Society established under Article 12 of the Framework Act on Intelligent Informatization;
  6. Any other institution or organization recognized by the Minister of Science and ICT as having specialized personnel and dedicated organizations related to quantum science and technology or the quantum industry.
  (2) Where the Minister of Science and ICT entrusts the task under paragraph (1), the Minister shall publish the person entrusted with the task and the details of the entrusted task in the Official Gazette.

Article 10 (Analysis and review of impact of quantum science and technology and response measures) (1) The impact analysis on quantum science and technology conducted under Article 10(1) of the Act shall be conducted using the following methods:
  1. Literature reviews regarding the state of development in quantum science and technology and the quantum industry, their application areas, and their impact on the affairs under the relevant jurisdiction;
  2. Assessments of the impact of quantum science and technology on current science and technology, national security, and the national economy;
  3. Scenario analyses comparing conditions before and after the introduction of quantum science and technology;
  4. Cost-benefit analyses quantitatively and qualitatively comparing the costs and benefits arising from the introduction of quantum science and technology into areas, such as science and technology, industry, and national security, related to the affairs under the relevant jurisdiction;
  5. Surveys conducted among experts in quantum science and technology or the quantum industry on the impact on the affairs under the relevant jurisdiction;
  6. Risk analyses on technical and economic issues, etc. that may arise from the introduction of quantum science and technology.
  (2) The head of the relevant central administrative agency shall consider the following matters when reviewing security threat factors to the public and private sectors arising from the development of quantum science and technology under Article 10(2) of the Act:
  1. To review whether the confidentiality, integrity, accountability, and availability of the information security system defined in Article 2(1)1 of the Act on the Promotion of Information Security Industry and the Information and Communications defined in Article 2(1)1 of the Special Act on Information and Communications Promotion and Convergence Activation are ensured, and whether authentication and non-repudiation are possible;
  2. To review response measures to security threat factors and the effectiveness of the response measures.
  (3) The heads of relevant central administrative agencies may support the development and validation of related technologies, pilot projects, and demonstration, among others, in order to effectively promote the following matters:
  1. Impact analyses on the spillover effects of quantum science and technology conducted under Article 10(1) of the Act;
  2. Review of security threat factors to the public and private sectors under Article 10(2) of the Act;
  3. Response measures under Article 10(3) of the Act.
  (4) The heads of relevant central administrative agencies shall submit the following matters to the Minister of Science and ICT to ensure that they are reflected in the comprehensive quantum plan and implementation plan under Article 10(3) of the Act:
  1. Results of analysis and review conducted under Article 10(1) and (2) of the Act;
  2. Response measures prepared under Article 10(3) of the Act;

Article 11 (Technology roadmap) (1) The Minister of Science and ICT shall prepare a technology roadmap for the field of quantum science and technology under Article 11(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "technology roadmap") every 2 years and notify the heads of relevant central administrative agencies thereof.
  (2) The technology roadmap shall include the following matters:
  1. Concepts and scope;
  2. Survey and analysis of technology demand and trends;
  3. Prospects for technological development (including the timing of market diffusion);
  4. Selection of target technologies;
  5. Details of technology development by stage of quantum science and technology advancement;
  6. Strategies for securing technologies (including capabilities and constraint factors);
  7. Trends in domestic and international technology-related patents.
  (3) The Minister of Science and ICT deems it necessary in light of advances in quantum science and technology, the Minister may revise or supplement the technology roadmap.
  (4) Where the Minister of Science and ICT revises or supplements the technology roadmap under paragraph (3), the Minister shall notify the heads of the relevant central administrative agencies thereof.

Article 12 (Requirements for designation of institutions dedicated to commercialization) (1) An institution seeking designation as a dedicated institution under Article 14(2) of the Act shall meet all of the following requirements:
  1. It shall have a dedicated organization for the quantum industry with at least 5 full-time employees;
  2. It shall have dedicated personnel for the quantum industry, including impact analyses of quantum science and technology and responses to security threats under Article 10 of the Act;
  3. It shall have a track record of commercializing technology development outcomes or a track record of commercialization in the quantum industry.
  (2) Where the head of a relevant central administrative agency designates a dedicated institution in accordance with Article 14(2) of the Act or revokes the designation of a dedicated institution in accordance with paragraph (4) of that Article, he or she shall post the fact on the website of the relevant central administrative agency.

Article 13 (Performance evaluation of institutions dedicated to commercialization) (1) When evaluating the performance of a dedicated institution under Article 14(3) of the Act, the head of the relevant central administrative agency shall formulate an evaluation plan including the following matters:
  1. General directions for performance evaluation;
  2. Methods of performance evaluation;
  3. Procedures for performance evaluation;
  4. Other matters necessary for performance evaluation.
  (2) The head of the relevant central administrative agency shall notify the evaluation plan formulated under paragraph (1) to the dedicated institution and post it on the website of the central administrative agency concerned.
  (3) The head of the relevant central administrative agency may establish and operate an evaluation panel including experts with specialized knowledge and extensive experience in technology commercialization, quantum science and technology, and the quantum industry, in order to conduct performance evaluations objectively and efficiently.

Article 14 (Promotion of standardization) (1) “Programs prescribed by Presidential Decree” in Article 15(1)4 of the Act means the following programs:
  1. Planning, evaluation, management, and diffusion of programs related to standardization in the fields of quantum science and technology and the quantum Industry;
  2. Establishment of an information system related to standards in the fields of quantum science and technology and the quantum industry;
  3. Support for the application or utilization of standards in the fields of quantum science and technology and the quantum industry;
  4. Promotion of cooperation with standards-related enterprises in the fields of quantum science and technology and the quantum industry;
  5. Public relations, education, training, exhibition, and other activities related to standards in the fields of quantum science and technology and the quantum industry;
  6. Support for the creation of standard-essential patents in the fields of quantum science and technology and the quantum industry.
  (2) An entity seeking designation as a specialized institution under Article 15(2) of the Act shall meet all of the following requirements:
  1. It shall be a public institution as defined in Article 4 of the Act on the Management of Public Institutions or a non-profit corporation established under Article 32 of the Civil Act;
  2. It shall have dedicated personnel, an organizational structure, and operational systems for implementing the programs under Article 15(1) of the Act;
  3. It shall have a track record of establishing, revising, abolishing, and disseminating standards;
  4. It shall have a track record of specialized surveys, research, consulting, education, or other activities related to standardization.
  (3) Where the head of a relevant central administrative agency designates a specialized institution in accordance with Article 15(2) of the Act or revokes the designation of a specialized institution in accordance with paragraph (4) of that Article, he or she shall post the fact on the website of the relevant central administrative agency.

Article 15 (Start-up and enterprise development) (1) An institution or organization seeking designation as a dedicated institution under Article 16(2) of the Act shall be any of the following:
  1. A public institution as defined in Article 4 of the Act on the Management of Public Institutions;
  2. A non-profit corporation established under Article 32 of the Civil Act that engages in activities related to the quantum industry.
  (2) Where the head of a relevant central administrative agency designates a dedicated institution in accordance with Article 16(2) of the Act or revokes the designation of a dedicated institution in accordance with paragraph (3) of that Article, he or she shall post the fact on the website of the relevant central administrative agency.

Article 16 (Support for operation of quantum fabs) (1) “Criteria prescribed by Presidential Decree, including specialized operational personnel and facility utilization rates” in Article 17(2) of the Act means the following criteria:
  1. Specialized personnel holding a doctoral degree in a process-related field of quantum science and technology or the quantum industry, or possessing at least 10 years of professional experience in the field;
  2. Quantitative utilization rate of the quantum fab;
  3. Research outcomes achieved through the utilization of the quantum fab.
  (2) The evaluation of the performance of a quantum fab conducted under Article 17(3) of the Act (hereafter referred to as "performance evaluation" in this Article) shall be conducted comprehensively on the basis of written evaluations, the solicitation of expert opinions, and other methods in accordance with the following criteria:
  1. The current status of specialized personnel holding a doctoral degree in a process-related field of quantum science and technology or the quantum industry, or possessing at least 10 years of professional experience in the field, including the number of the personnel, whether they are full-time employees, and their length of service;
  2. The number of cases of external utilization involving domestic experts;
  3. Research outcomes achieved through the utilization of the quantum fab;
  4. Transparency in the operation of the quantum fab;
  5. Results of a user satisfaction survey on the quantum fab;
  6. Other matters deemed necessary by the Minister of Science and ICT.
  (3) Where the subject of the performance evaluation is required to undergo phase evaluations and a final evaluation under Article 12(2) of the National Research and Development and Innovation Act, the phase evaluations and final evaluation may substitute for the performance evaluation.

Article 17 (Designation of quantum science and technology research centers) (1) “Institution prescribed by Presidential Decree” under Article 18 (1) 5 of the Act means an institution that meets all of the following requirements:
  1. It shall have a separate dedicated organization for securing source technologies in the field of quantum science and technology and linking them to the quantum industry;
  2. It shall have at least 20 specialized personnel holding doctoral degrees in fields related to quantum science and technology;
  3. It shall be equipped with the necessary equipment for conducting research;
  4. It shall have research achievements related to quantum science technology, such as theses and patents;
  5. It shall facilitate linkage and convergence with adjacent technological fields.
  (2) Before designating a quantum science and technology research center under Article 18(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "quantum research center"), the head of the relevant central administrative agency shall formulate a plan for the designation of a quantum research center, taking into consideration the designation requirements specified in paragraph (1) and post the plan on the website of the relevant central administrative agency.
  (3) Where a quantum research center subject to the performance review conducted under Article 18(2) of the Act is required to undergo phase evaluations and a final evaluation under Article 12(2) of the National Research and Development Innovation Act, the phase evaluations and final evaluation may substitute for the performance review.
  (4) Where the head of a relevant central administrative agency designates a quantum research center in accordance with Article 18(1) of the Act or revokes the designation of a quantum research center in accordance with paragraph (4) of that Article, he or she shall post the fact on the website of the relevant central administrative agency.

Article 18 (Encouragement of dissemination of quantum science and technology culture) (1) The head of a relevant central administrative agency intending to conduct any of the programs listed in the subparagraphs of Article 19(1) of the Act shall submit the plan to the Minister of Science and ICT.
  (2) The Minister of Science and ICT shall reflect the plans submitted under paragraph (1) in the implementation plan.
  (3) The heads of relevant central administrative agencies may jointly conduct the programs listed in the subparagraphs of Article 19(1) of the Act.

Article 19 (Support for specialized educational institutions for quantum science and technology) “ Universities and graduate schools equipped with specialized personnel and facilities as prescribed by Presidential Decree” in Article 22(1) of the Act means any of the universities and graduate schools meeting all of the following requirements:
  1. It shall have a department, academic department, or equivalent organizational unit or major related to quantum science and technology;
  2. The university, graduate school, or consortium of universities and graduate schools shall have at least 15 faculty members or other specialized personnel holding doctoral degrees in quantum science and technology;
  3. It shall have research achievements related to quantum science and technology, including academic papers and patents, produced by the specialized personnel under subparagraph 2;
  4. It shall enable joint research and human resource development with adjacent academic fields, thereby facilitating linkage and convergence between quantum science and technology and adjacent academic fields.

Article 20 (Formulation of master plans for quantum clusters) (1) The head of a relevant central administrative agency who receives a request from the Minister of Science and ICT for consultation regarding the master plan for quantum clusters under Article 24(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "master plan for quantum clusters") in accordance with under Article 24(3) of the Act, the head of the relevant central administrative agency shall reply with an opinion within 20 days from the date of receiving the request.
  (2) “Where any modification concerns minor matters prescribed by Presidential Decree” in the proviso of Article 24(5) of the Act means any of the following cases:
  1. Where it is intended to modify the master plan for quantum clusters to the extent not to change the purpose and performance indicators of the master plan for quantum clusters, the deadlines for achieving the objectives, etc.;
  2. Where it is intended to change terms, etc. in accordance with the amendment or change of other statutes, regulations, plans, etc.;
  3. Where it is intended to correct a simple mistake, misrepresentation, omission, or obvious error corresponding thereto.
  (3) Where the Minister of Science and ICT formulates a master plan for quantum clusters, the Minister shall post the contents thereof on the website of the Ministry of Science and ICT.
  (4) The Minister of Science and ICT shall report to the Quantum Strategy Committee on the results of implementation of the master plan for quantum clusters and the results of performance review conducted under Article 24(6) of the Act.
  (5) The Minister of Science and ICT shall post the implementation results and performance of the master plan for quantum clusters on the website of the Ministry of Science and ICT in accordance with Article 24(6) of the Act.

Article 21 (Formulation of quantum cluster development plans and designation of quantum clusters) (1) In order to designate a quantum cluster, the Minister of Science and ICT shall prepare guidelines for formulating a quantum cluster development plan under Article 25(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "quantum cluster development plan") and publish the guidelines in the Official Gazette, and notify the Special Metropolitan City Mayor, Metropolitan City Mayors, Special Self-Governing City Mayor, Do Governors, and Special Self-Governing Province Governors (hereinafter referred to as "Mayors/Do Governors") thereof.
  (2) Any of the Mayors/Do Governors who intends to have a quantum cluster designated shall prepare the opinion of the relevant Special Metropolitan City, Metropolitan City, Special Self-Governing City, Do, or Special Self-Governing Province (hereinafter referred to as "City/Do") in the form of a City/Do quantum development plan (hereinafter referred to as "City/Do quantum development plan") and submit the form to the Minister of Science and ICT.
  (3) The Minister of Science and ICT shall review the City/Do quantum cluster development plan submitted under paragraph (2) in accordance with the following requirements and designate a quantum cluster:
  1. Whether the City/Do quantum cluster development plan is consistent with the basic objectives of the establishment of quantum clusters and mid- to long-term development directions under Article 24(2)1 of the Act;
  2. Whether the enterprises, universities, and research institutes participating in the quantum cluster possess sufficient capabilities in relation to quantum science and technology and the quantum industry, including performance records in academic publications, patents, and standards, human resources, and facilities in possession, as well as efforts for joint utilization, commercialization, international cooperation;
  3. Whether the City/Do’s support plan and direction for development are appropriate to support capacity enhancement and mutual linkage activities among enterprises, universities, research institutes, and other entities participating in the quantum cluster under Article 24(2)3 of the Act;
  4. Whether the target performance of the quantum cluster and its performance management measures are appropriate;
  5. Whether the operational plan for the quantum cluster is appropriate;
  6. Whether the cooperation plan among the quantum clusters is appropriate;
  7. Other matters deemed necessary by the Minister of Science and ICT.
  (4) Where the Minister of Science and ICT designates a quantum cluster, the Minister shall reflect the City/Do quantum cluster development plan submitted under paragraph (2) in the quantum cluster development plan formulated by the Minister of Science and ICT.
  (5) Where the head of a relevant central administrative agency receives a request from the Minister of Science and ICT for consultation regarding a quantum cluster development plan or the designation of a quantum cluster under Article 25(1) of the Act, he or she shall reply his or her opinion within 20 days from the date of receiving the request.
  (6) Where the Minister of Science and ICT publishes the results of designation of a quantum cluster in the Official Gazette under the former part of Article 25(3) of the Act, the Minister shall include the following matters:
  1. The name, location, and size of the quantum cluster;
  2. The purpose and date of designation of the quantum cluster;
  3. Topographical drawing of the quantum cluster;
  4. Other matters deemed necessary by the Minister of Science and ICT.

Article 22 (Performance review of quantum clusters) The Minister of Science and ICT shall publish on the website of the Ministry of Science and ICT the results of reviewing the operational status and performance quantum clusters notified under the former part of Article 27(1)of the Act and shall reflect the results in the implementation plan for the following year.

Article 23 (Re-examination of regulation) The Minister of Science and ICT shall examine the appropriateness of the following matters every 3 years, counting from January 1, 2025 (referring to the period that ends on the day before January 1st of every 3rd year) and shall take measures, such as making improvements:
  1. Requirements for designation as a dedicated institution for commercialization under Article 12;
  2. Requirements for designation as a specialized institution for standardization programs under Article 14;
  3. Requirements for designation as a dedicated institution for startup and enterprise development under Article 15;
  4. Requirements for designation as a quantum research center under Article 17.

